hecking"}], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2021, 4, 27]], "date-time": "2021-04-27T21:49:06Z", "timestamp": 1619560146000}, "score": 26.45951, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://link.springer.com/10.1007/3-7643-7319-9_5"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "ISBN": ["3764372176"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-7643-7319-9_5"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 5]], "date-time": "2024-05-05T21:06:05Z", "timestamp": 1714943165013}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Palgrave Macmillan", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781137339812", "type": "print"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.1057/9781137339812.0013", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2015, 6, 8]], "date-time": "2015-06-08T11:25:01Z", "timestamp": 1433762701000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Simulating an Interbank Payment System"], "prefix": "10.1057", "author": [{"given": "Pietro", "family": "Terna", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "297", "container-title": ["Agent-based Models of the Economy"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2015, 6, 8]], "date-time": "2015-06-08T15:14:04Z", "timestamp": 1433776444000}, "score": 25.80008, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "http://www.palgraveconnect.com/doifinder/10.1057/9781137339812.0013"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[null]]}, "ISBN": ["9781137339812"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.1057/9781137339812.0013"}, {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]], "date-time": "2026-02-02T16:13:46Z", "timestamp": 1770048826619, "version": "3.49.0"}, "posted": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 30]]}, "group-title": "Computer Science and Mathematics", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "MDPI AG", "license": [{"start": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 30]], "date-time": "2026-01-30T00:00:00Z", "timestamp": 1769731200000}, "content-version": "unspecified", "delay-in-days": 0, "URL": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "accepted": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 29]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>The scarcity of high-quality, labeled audio data for legal proceedings remains a significant barrier to developing robust speech-to-text and speaker diarization systems for the judiciary. This paper in- troduces Deepcounsel, a high-fidelity synthetic speech dataset simulating courtroom environments. Utilizing a multi-agent system powered by the Gemini 2.5 Pro model, we orchestrated complex interactions between eleven distinct roles, including judges, attor- neys, witnesses, and court staff. By leveraging native multimodal generation, Deepcounsel provides a diverse range of legal termi- nology, emotional prosody, and multi-speaker overlaps. Our results demonstrate that synthetic datasets generated via multi-agent Large Language Models (LLMs) can serve as a viable proxy for training specialized legal AI models where real-world data is restricted by privacy laws.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.20944/preprints202601.2417.v1", "type": "posted-content", "created": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]], "date-time": "2026-02-02T05:09:43Z", "timestamp": 1770008983000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Deepcounsel: A Multi-Agent Framework for Simulating Complex Courtroom Audio Environments"], "prefix": "10.20944", "author": [{"ORCID": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7190-5040", "authenticated-orcid": false, "given": "Aniket", "family": "Deroy", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "1968", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2026, 2, 2]], "date-time": "2026-02-02T05:10:19Z", "timestamp": 1770009019000}, "score": 25.795166, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202601.2417/v1"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2026, 1, 30]]}, "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.20944/prepr